  "title": "Physical quantities, units and uncertainties",
  "main_stem": null,
  "parts": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "In the following list, underline all units that are SI base units.\n\nampere      degree Celsius      kilogram      newton",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(i)",
      "part_stem": "Fig. 1.1 shows a horizontal beam clamped at one end with a block attached to the other end. {{figure:fig_1_1}}\n\nFig. 1.1\n\nThe block is made to oscillate vertically.\n\nThe Young modulus $E$ of the material of the beam is given by $$E = \\frac{kM}{T^2}$$ where $M$ is the mass of the block, $T$ is the period of the oscillations and $k$ is a constant.\n\nA student determines the values and percentage uncertainties of $k$, $M$ and $T$. Table 1.1 lists the percentage uncertainties.\n\nTable 1.1\n\n| quantity | percentage uncertainty |\n| $k$ | $\\pm 2.1\\%$ |\n| $M$ | $\\pm 0.6\\%$ |\n| $T$ | $\\pm 1.5\\%$ |\n\nThe student uses the values of $k$, $M$ and $T$ to calculate the value of $E$ as $8.245 \\times 10^9$Pa.",
      "text": "(i) Calculate the percentage uncertainty in the value of $E$.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": "percentage uncertainty =",
      "unit": "%"
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "(ii) Use your answer in (b)(i) to determine the value of $E$, with its absolute uncertainty, to an appropriate number of significant figures.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": "$E = ($",
      "unit": "$\\times 10^9$Pa"
    }
  ],
  "markscheme": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "ampere and kilogram underlined, no others"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(i)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "2.1 + 0.6 + (2 \u00d7 1.5)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "5.7%"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "absolute uncertainty = 0.057 \u00d7 8.245 \u00d7 10^9 (= 0.47 \u00d7 10^9 Pa)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "E = (8.25 \u00b1 0.47) \u00d7 10^9 Pa to 3 s.f."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
